<title>UK: John Lewis store sales rose 11.4% in week.</title>
<headline>John Lewis store sales rose 11.4% in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK weekly department store sales rose 11.4 percent in the week to May 24 from the same week a year earlier. In the 17 weeks to May 24, they were up 9.5 percent.</p>
<p>Total sales, including the Waitrose supermarket group, rose 7.6 percent in the latest week and 7.0 percent in the 17 week period.</p>
<p>-- Michael Peacock, London newsroom 44 171 542 7708</p>
